{"toolCallId":"call_90636912e8df4b51820eb190355aa64c","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"[What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain point.]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag\"\n  - \"add a quiet flag to recommend level sh\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.2 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\n[2-3 sentence high-level overview for stakeholders who need quick context]\n\n**Key Decisions**: [Major decision 1], [Major decision 2]\n\n**Critical Dependencies**: [Blocking dependency]\n\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 3 |\n| **Priority** | [P0/P1/P2] |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n[What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain point.]\n\n### Purpose\n[One-sentence outcome statement. What does success look like?]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- [Deliverable 1]\n- [Deliverable 2]\n- [Deliverable 3]\n\n### Out of Scope\n- [Excluded item 1] - [why]\n- [Excluded item 2] - [why]\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| [path/to/file.js] | [Modify/Create/Delete] | [Brief description] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | [Requirement description] |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-002 | [Requirement description] |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: [Primary measurable outcome]\n- **SC-002**: [Secondary measurable outcome]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | [System/API] | [What if blocked] | [Fallback plan] |\n| Risk | [Risk description] | [High/Med/Low] | [Mitigation strategy] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: [Response time target - e.g., <200ms p95]\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: [Auth requirement - e.g., JWT tokens required]\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: [Uptime target - e.g., 99.9%]\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- Empty input: [How system handles]\n- Maximum length: [Limit and behavior]\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- External service failure: [Fallback behavior]\n- Network timeout: [Retry strategy]\n\n---\n\n## 9. COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n\n| Dimension | Score | Triggers |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Scope | [/25] | [Files: X, LOC: Y, Systems: Z] |\n| Risk | [/25] | [Auth: Y/N, API: Y/N, Breaking: Y/N] |\n| Research | [/20] | [Investigation needs] |\n| Multi-Agent | [/15] | [Workstreams: X] |\n| Coordination | [/15] | [Dependencies: X] |\n| **Total** | **[/100]** | **Level 3** |\n\n---\n\n## 10. RISK MATRIX\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | [Risk] | [H/M/L] | [H/M/L] | [Strategy] |\n\n---\n\n## 11. USER STORIES\n\n### US-001: [Title] (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** [user type], **I want** [needed behavior], **so that** [benefit].\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n### US-002: [Title] (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** [user type], **I want** [needed behavior], **so that** [benefit].\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- [Question 1 requiring clarification]\n- [Question 2 requiring clarification]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See `decision-record.md`\n\n---\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"recommend-level.sh prints a multi-section report, so a caller that only needs the level has to filter it. Add a --quiet flag that prints the single Recommended Level line and leaves every existing output path unchanged.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag\"\n  - \"add a quiet flag to recommend level sh\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.2 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\n`recommend-level.sh` scores a task and prints a report: a level line, the score and confidence, a factor breakdown, and a phase recommendation. An agent or shell pipeline that only needs the level has to grep that report. `--quiet` adds one output mode that prints exactly the existing level line and nothing else; without the flag the script behaves as it does today.\n\n**Key Decisions**: `--quiet` reuses the `Recommended Level: N (Name)` line verbatim; `--quiet` outranks `--json` when both are passed; no `-q` alias in this packet.\n\n**Critical Dependencies**: Bash 3.2 compatibility, because the script runs on macOS's default shell. No new runtime dependency.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 3 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | detached HEAD (7433813f54) |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\nThe default text output is a report of 16 to 17 lines: a leading blank line, `Recommended Level: N (Name)`, `Score: X/100 | Confidence: Y%`, a six-row factor breakdown, and a phase recommendation section. A caller that needs the level — an agent choosing between a Level 1 and a Level 3 packet, or a shell pipeline — must grep or parse the line out of that report. `--json` is not a substitute because it emits a multi-field object that needs a JSON parser. The flag does not exist today: `recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet` prints `ERROR: Unknown option: --quiet` and exits 1.\n\n### Purpose\nAdd one flag that prints the final recommended-level line and nothing else, without changing any existing output path.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Accept `--quiet` in the argument parser and record it in a quiet-mode global.\n- Print exactly `Recommended Level: ${RECOMMENDED_LEVEL} (${LEVEL_NAME})` plus a trailing newline when quiet mode is on.\n- Give quiet mode precedence over `--json` when both flags are passed.\n- Document the flag in the script's header comment and in `show_help()`.\n- Cover the new mode with a bash test harness beside the existing `test-upgrade-level.sh`.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- A `-q` short alias - not requested by this feature, and it widens the surface without a caller. Recorded as ADR-003.\n- Changing the wording, spacing or fields of the level line - callers already grep it.\n- Suppressing stderr diagnostics - errors stay visible and keep exit 1.\n- Changes to scoring, thresholds, phase logic or JSON fields.\n- Fixing the stale positional-argument examples in `execution-methods.md` - a separate defect for a separate packet.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Modify | Add `QUIET_MODE`, the `--quiet` case branch, `output_quiet()`, dispatch precedence, and help text in both help surfaces |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh` | Create | Bash harness pinning the quiet contract and the unchanged default path |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/execution-methods.md` | Modify | Add `--quiet` to the recommend-level flag table |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | `--quiet` is accepted and turns quiet mode on: no unknown-option error, exit 0 on valid inputs. |\n| REQ-002 | With `--quiet`, stdout is exactly one line, `Recommended Level: N (Name)` plus a trailing newline: no leading blank line, no score, no breakdown, no phase section. |\n| REQ-003 | Without `--quiet`, stdout is byte-identical to the pre-change output for the same arguments. |\n| REQ-004 | `--quiet` outranks `--json`; `--quiet --json` prints the same single line and no JSON document. |\n| REQ-005 | Both help surfaces list `--quiet` with a one-line description. |\n| REQ-006 | Errors keep going to stderr with exit 1 under `--quiet`; quiet mode never swallows a diagnostic. |\n| REQ-007 | `--help` and `-h` still print the full help text and exit 0, with or without `--quiet`. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-008 | The level number and name printed under `--quiet` match the non-quiet run for the same inputs, including the Level 0 and Level 3 boundaries. |\n| REQ-009 | A bash test harness covers quiet output, default-output regression, precedence, help and error paths. |\n| REQ-010 | `execution-methods.md` names the flag in its recommend-level flag table. |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: `recommend-level.sh --loc 200 --files 5 --api --quiet` prints exactly `Recommended Level: 1 (Baseline)` and exits 0.\n- **SC-002**: The default-output capture for a fixed argument set is unchanged byte for byte against the pre-change capture.\n- **SC-003**: `recommend-level.sh --loc 200 --files 5 --api --quiet --json` prints the same single line and contains no `{`.\n- **SC-004**: `recommend-level.sh --quiet --bogus` exits 1 and writes `ERROR: Unknown option: --bogus` to stderr, with empty stdout.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | Bash 3.2 or newer | The script must keep running on macOS's default shell | Avoid bash-4-only syntax; run the harness under `/bin/bash` |\n| Risk | Precedence between `--quiet` and `--json` is unstated | Med | ADR-002 fixes precedence; a test pins the combination |\n| Risk | A leading blank line leaks into quiet output | Med | `output_quiet()` uses a single `printf '%s\\n'`; the test compares exact content and line count |\n| Risk | Help text drifts between the header comment and `show_help()` | Low | One task edits both; the test asserts both list the flag |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: Quiet mode adds no measurable work: one `printf` replaces roughly a dozen `echo` calls, so wall time stays at or below the current run for the same inputs.\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: No new input surface. The mode prints only values the script already computed and already prints in its report.\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: Quiet output is deterministic for fixed inputs and independent of the phase-scoring flags.\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- Neither `--loc` nor `--files`: the existing validation error wins; quiet mode writes nothing to stdout and exits 1.\n- Level 0 and Level 3: the same line format, with the level name from `determine_level`.\n- Repeated `--quiet`: idempotent; one line.\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- `--quiet --json`: one line, no JSON document.\n- `--quiet --help`: full help text, exit 0.\n- `--quiet --no-recommend-phases`: one line; the phase section is already suppressed.\n- Unknown option with `--quiet`: stderr diagnostic and exit 1, unchanged.\n- Closed stdout, such as `| head -0`: existing shell behaviour, no new handling.\n\n---\n\n## 9. COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n\n| Dimension | Score | Triggers |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Scope | 8/25 | Files: 3, LOC: ~35, Systems: 1 |\n| Risk | 4/25 | Auth: N, API: N, Breaking: N (output contract only) |\n| Research | 2/20 | Script read end to end; no open unknowns |\n| Multi-Agent | 2/15 | Workstreams: 1 |\n| Coordination | 2/15 | Dependencies: 0 |\n| **Total** | **18/100** | **Level 3 declared** |\n\nThe scoring algorithm maps 18/100 to Level 0. This packet is Level 3 because `create.sh --level 3` was specified for the authoring task, not because the change is architecturally complex. Scope stays one script, one test file and one documentation row.\n\n---\n\n## 10. RISK MATRIX\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | Two callers read quiet/JSON precedence differently | M | L | ADR-002 fixes the rule; AC-005 pins it |\n| R-002 | The default report drifts while the new path is added | M | L | Pre-change captures in `scratch/baseline/` and a byte diff in AC-003 and AC-004 |\n| R-003 | Only one help surface learns about the flag | L | M | One task edits both; AC-006 asserts both |\n| R-004 | Quiet mode suppresses a diagnostic by mistake | L | L | AC-007 asserts empty stdout and the error text on stderr |\n\n---\n\n## 11. USER STORIES\n\n### US-001: One-line level for an agent (Priority: P0)\n\n**As an** agent deciding whether a task needs a Level 1 or a Level 3 packet, **I want** the recommender to print only the level line, **so that** I can read the value without grepping a report.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (AC-001, AC-002, AC-009).\n\n---\n\n### US-002: Existing readers see no change (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** maintainer of anything that reads the current report, **I want** the default text and JSON output to stay byte-identical, **so that** the new flag costs no downstream edit.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (AC-003, AC-004).\n\n---\n\n### US-003: Predictable combined flags (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** script author, **I want** a stated rule for `--quiet --json`, **so that** passing both does not depend on flag order or guesswork.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (AC-005).\n\n---\n\n### US-004: Discoverable flag (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** future contributor, **I want** `--quiet` in the script's help and in the workflow reference, **so that** I can find it without reading the case block.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (AC-006, AC-011).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- None. ADR-001 through ADR-003 in `plan.md` record the three decisions this feature needed.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Acceptance Criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":87,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":45}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_92120c6e3b974ffd965863c9fed23e50","title":"Ran echo","kind":"execute","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"resource","resource":{"mimeType":"text/x-shellscript","text":"for f in spec plan tasks acceptance-criteria; do echo \"$f: $(wc -l < specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/$f.md) lines, $(wc -c < specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/$f.md) bytes\"; done; echo \"impl-summary body lines 25-100 unchanged check:\"; sed -n '25,30p' specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/implementation-summary.md","uri":"tool://preview"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/preview_is_shell_command":true}}}],"rawInput":{"command":"for f in spec plan tasks acceptance-criteria; do echo \"$f: $(wc -l < specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/$f.md) lines, $(wc -c < specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/$f.md) bytes\"; done; echo \"impl-summary body lines 25-100 unchanged check:\"; sed -n '25,30p' specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/implementation-summary.md","workdir":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/commandNames":["echo"],"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_9231278a20874d97b3d9ee46c6bc541d","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add a third output mode to recommend-level.sh: a --quiet flag that prints only the Recommended Level line. The change touches the argument parser, one new output function and the dispatch tail; scoring is untouched.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.2 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2-compatible shell |\n| **Framework** | None; one script, no sourced project library |\n| **Storage** | None |\n| **Testing** | Bash harness in `runtime/cli/tests/`, byte-diff captures, and `shellcheck` at `/opt/homebrew/bin/shellcheck` |\n\n### Overview\n`recommend-level.sh` already separates scoring from presentation: the scoring functions fill globals, and a dispatch tail chooses `output_text` or `output_json`. This change adds a third writer, `output_quiet`, and a `QUIET_MODE` global set by a `--quiet` case branch. The dispatch checks quiet first, so the flag prints the same level line the text report carries and nothing else. No scoring function changes.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [x] Problem statement and scope documented in `spec.md` §2 and §3\n- [x] Success criteria measurable in `spec.md` §5 and `acceptance-criteria.md`\n- [x] Dependencies identified in §6 of this plan\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh` exits 0 with zero failures\n- [ ] Default text and JSON captures diff clean against `scratch/baseline/`\n- [ ] Spec, plan and tasks agree on the final behavior\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nSingle-file CLI script with a dispatch tail. There is no framework, no service layer and no stored state; the script computes in memory and writes once.\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument parser** (`recommend-level.sh:652-719`): a `while`/`case` loop that sets `LOC`, `FILES` and the risk flags and rejects unknown options. It gains the `--quiet` branch.\n- **Scoring pipeline** (`recommend-level.sh:216-500`): `calculate_loc_score`, `calculate_files_score`, `calculate_risk_score`, `calculate_complexity_score`, `determine_level`, `calculate_confidence`, `determine_phasing`. Unchanged.\n- **Output writers** (`recommend-level.sh:508-648`): `output_text` and `output_json` today; this packet adds `output_quiet` beside them.\n- **Dispatch tail** (`recommend-level.sh:770-774`): selects one writer and exits 0. This is the only control-flow change.\n\n### Data Flow\n`argv` → parser sets inputs and mode globals → scoring fills `TOTAL_SCORE`, `RECOMMENDED_LEVEL`, `LEVEL_NAME`, `CONFIDENCE` and the phase fields → dispatch picks one writer → stdout → `exit 0`. Quiet mode changes only the writer choice, so every value the line carries is the value the report already carries.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `recommend-level.sh` argument parser | Accepts 11 flags and rejects every other token with exit 1 | update: add `--quiet` after the `--json|-j` branch at `recommend-level.sh:706-709` | `grep -n -- '--quiet' recommend-level.sh` shows the case branch; `--quiet` run exits 0 |\n| `output_text` | Prints the 16-17 line report | unchanged | byte diff against `scratch/baseline/text-*.txt` |\n| `output_json` | Prints the JSON document | unchanged | byte diff against `scratch/baseline/json-*.json` |\n| new `output_quiet` | Prints one line | create beside `output_text` at `recommend-level.sh:508` | harness asserts exact content, line count and no leading blank line |\n| dispatch tail | Chooses text or JSON | update: quiet branch first at `recommend-level.sh:770-774` | `--quiet --json` harness case |\n| `show_help` OPTIONS | Lists the flags | update at `recommend-level.sh:181` | `bash recommend-level.sh --help \\| grep -c -- '--quiet'` returns `1` |\n| header comment OPTIONS | Lists the flags for readers of the file | update at `recommend-level.sh:26` | `grep -c -- '^#   --quiet' recommend-level.sh` returns `1` |\n| `execution-methods.md` flag table | Documents the scoring flags | update one row | `grep -c -- '--quiet' execution-methods.md` returns `1` |\n| In-repo callers of the script | None read its stdout | not a consumer | `grep -rn \"Recommended Level\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit` returns 0 hits outside `recommend-level.sh` |\n| `-q` short flag | Not present; `-q` exits 1 as unknown | unchanged | ADR-003; harness asserts `-q` still fails |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `grep -rln \"QUIET_MODE\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/*.sh` returns `check-completion.sh`, `progressive-validate.sh` and `validate.sh`. Each owns its own parser; there is no shared flag table, so this change adds one branch to one parser rather than updating a central list.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `grep -rn \"Recommended Level\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit` returns 0 hits outside `recommend-level.sh`, so no in-repo script parses the line.\n- Matrix axes: output mode (text, json, quiet, quiet+json) crossed with phase scoring (on, off) gives 8 rows; level boundaries (0, 1, 3) add 3 rows in quiet mode. The harness covers all 11.\n- Algorithm invariant: quiet mode selects a writer and must not alter any computed value. Adversarial cases: a leading blank line, an extra trailing line, JSON leaking through, a diagnostic leaking to stdout, and an unknown option being swallowed.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\n### Phase 1: Baseline capture\nRun the current script for the three level-boundary argument sets and store stdout in `scratch/baseline/`. Nothing changes until those files exist, because every later regression claim compares against them.\n\n### Phase 2: Parser and output function\nAdd `QUIET_MODE=false` beside `JSON_OUTPUT=false`, the `--quiet` case branch after `--json|-j`, and `output_quiet()` beside `output_text`. The function prints one line through a single `printf '%s\\n'`, which rules out the leading blank line `output_text` starts with.\n\n### Phase 3: Dispatch and help\nReorder the dispatch tail so quiet mode is checked before JSON, then document the flag in both help surfaces: the header comment and `show_help()`.\n\n### Phase 4: Verification\nWrite and run `runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh`, diff both default captures, and run `shellcheck` on the script.\n\n### Phase 5: Documentation and closeout\nAdd the `--quiet` row to `execution-methods.md`, update `tasks.md` evidence, and record the outcome in `implementation-summary.md` at completion time.\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the task state and the verification checklist.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | `output_quiet` output shape and the parser branch | `runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh` |\n| Regression | Default text and JSON output, byte for byte | `diff` against `scratch/baseline/` |\n| Integration | Combined flags and exit codes in one shell | Harness cases for `--quiet --json`, `--quiet --help`, `--quiet --bogus` |\n| Manual | Read the help text and run one example by hand | Terminal |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| Bash 3.2 or newer | External | Green | The script stops running on macOS's default shell |\n| `test-upgrade-level.sh` harness pattern | Internal | Green | The new harness invents its own summary format and is harder to compare |\n| `shellcheck` | External tooling | Green | Lint step is skipped; the harness still gates behavior |\n| `scratch/baseline/` captures | Internal | Green | AC-003 and AC-004 lose their before-picture |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: Default text or JSON output changes, or quiet output is anything other than exactly one line.\n- **Procedure**: Revert the single implementation commit. The change is confined to one script, one new test file and one documentation row; there is no data, schema or configuration to unwind.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Baseline) ──► Phase 2 (Parser + writer) ──► Phase 3 (Dispatch + help)\n                                                              │\n                                                              ▼\n                                              Phase 4 (Verify) ──► Phase 5 (Docs)\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Baseline | None | Parser + writer, Docs |\n| Parser + writer | Baseline | Dispatch + help |\n| Dispatch + help | Parser + writer | Verify |\n| Verify | Dispatch + help | Docs |\n| Docs | Verify | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Baseline capture | Low | 15 minutes |\n| Parser + writer | Low | 30 minutes |\n| Dispatch + help | Low | 15 minutes |\n| Verification | Medium | 25 minutes |\n| Documentation | Low | 10 minutes |\n| **Total** | | **About 1.5 hours** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [x] No data changes; nothing to back up\n- [x] No feature flag to configure; the new flag is itself the opt-in\n- [x] No monitoring change; this is CLI stdout only\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. `git revert <implementation-sha>` on the branch that carries the change.\n2. Re-run `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh`.\n3. Confirm the default captures still diff clean against `scratch/baseline/`.\n4. No stakeholder notification is needed; the script is internal tooling.\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No.\n- **Reversal procedure**: N/A\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│  Baseline   │     │ Parser+Writer│    │ Dispatch+Help│\n└─────────────┘     └─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘\n                                               │\n                                        ┌──────▼──────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n                                        │   Phase 4   │────►│   Phase 5   │\n                                        │   Verify    │     │    Docs     │\n                                        └─────────────┘     └─────────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline captures | None | Text and JSON reference output | Harness regression cases |\n| `QUIET_MODE` global and parser branch | Baseline | Accepted `--quiet` | `output_quiet` dispatch |\n| `output_quiet` | Parser branch | One-line writer | Dispatch |\n| Dispatch branch | `output_quiet` | Quiet selection | Harness, help verification |\n| Help text | Parser branch | Documented flag | Help assertions |\n| Harness | All implementation pieces | PASS/FAIL evidence | Packet closure |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **T001 Baseline capture** - 15 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **T003 `output_quiet`** - 20 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **T004 Dispatch branch** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n4. **T007 Harness** - 25 minutes - CRITICAL\n5. **T010 Strict validation of this packet** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: About 80 minutes\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- T005 help text and T012 documentation row can run alongside the harness.\n- T001 baseline capture can run before any edit and does not block the parser edit.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Baseline captured | `scratch/baseline/` holds text and JSON captures for three argument sets | Phase 1 |\n| M2 | Quiet mode implemented | `--quiet` prints one line; default paths untouched | Phase 3 |\n| M3 | Verified | Harness exits 0, default diffs clean, `shellcheck` clean | Phase 4 |\n| M4 | Documented and closeable | `execution-methods.md` updated; every acceptance row `Met` | Phase 5 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: Quiet output reuses the existing level line verbatim\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: A caller needs the recommended level, and the report already carries it as `Recommended Level: N (Name)`. Any second format would become a second contract to keep in sync.\n\n**Decision**: `output_quiet()` prints the same `Recommended Level: N (Name)` line that `output_text` prints, followed by one newline, with no leading blank line.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Positive: one grep pattern works against both the report and the quiet output; no new vocabulary.\n- Negative: machine consumers still split on `:` and `(`. That cost already exists for the report, and the level number and name stay readable.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Print only the integer: hides the level name and breaks the line callers already match.\n- Keep the report and let callers filter it: that is the status quo this packet removes.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-002: `--quiet` takes precedence over `--json`\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: Both flags request a specific output shape, and the script accepts flags in any order. Combining them has no obvious meaning.\n\n**Decision**: Quiet mode wins. `--quiet --json` prints the one-line level and no JSON document.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Positive: the flag's promise is unconditional, so no combination silently produces a different shape.\n- Negative: a caller that passed both by mistake loses JSON without an error. The help text states the precedence, and AC-005 pins it.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Error on the combination: adds a failure mode for a case with an obvious reading.\n- JSON wins: contradicts the flag's stated contract.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-003: No `-q` short alias in this packet\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: `validate.sh`, `check-completion.sh` and `progressive-validate.sh` accept `--quiet|-q`. Adding `-q` here would match them, but no caller has asked for it.\n\n**Decision**: Add only `--quiet`, the requested surface.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Positive: the surface stays exactly as large as the feature, and no short flag is claimed before its meaning is needed.\n- Negative: a user who types `-q` gets an unknown-option error, which is inconsistent with the sibling scripts. A later packet can add the alias with a caller behind it.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Add `-q` now: unrequested surface, and the harness would then need to pin an alias nothing uses.\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add a third output mode to recommend-level.sh: a --quiet flag that prints only the Recommended Level line. The change touches the argument parser, one new output function and the dispatch tail; scoring is untouched.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.2 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2-compatible shell |\n| **Framework** | None; one script, no sourced project library |\n| **Storage** | None |\n| **Testing** | Bash harness in `runtime/cli/tests/`, byte-diff captures, and `shellcheck` at `/opt/homebrew/bin/shellcheck` |\n\n### Overview\n`recommend-level.sh` already separates scoring from presentation: the scoring functions fill globals, and a dispatch tail chooses `output_text` or `output_json`. This change adds a third writer, `output_quiet`, and a `QUIET_MODE` global set by a `--quiet` case branch. The dispatch checks quiet first, so the flag prints the same level line the text report carries and nothing else. No scoring function changes.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [x] Problem statement and scope documented in `spec.md` §2 and §3\n- [x] Success criteria measurable in `spec.md` §5 and `acceptance-criteria.md`\n- [x] Dependencies identified in §6 of this plan\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh` exits 0 with zero failures\n- [ ] Default text and JSON captures diff clean against `scratch/baseline/`\n- [ ] Spec, plan and tasks agree on the final behavior\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nSingle-file CLI script with a dispatch tail. There is no framework, no service layer and no stored state; the script computes in memory and writes once.\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument parser** (`recommend-level.sh:652-719`): a `while`/`case` loop that sets `LOC`, `FILES` and the risk flags and rejects unknown options. It gains the `--quiet` branch.\n- **Scoring pipeline** (`recommend-level.sh:216-500`): `calculate_loc_score`, `calculate_files_score`, `calculate_risk_score`, `calculate_complexity_score`, `determine_level`, `calculate_confidence`, `determine_phasing`. Unchanged.\n- **Output writers** (`recommend-level.sh:508-648`): `output_text` and `output_json` today; this packet adds `output_quiet` beside them.\n- **Dispatch tail** (`recommend-level.sh:770-774`): selects one writer and exits 0. This is the only control-flow change.\n\n### Data Flow\n`argv` → parser sets inputs and mode globals → scoring fills `TOTAL_SCORE`, `RECOMMENDED_LEVEL`, `LEVEL_NAME`, `CONFIDENCE` and the phase fields → dispatch picks one writer → stdout → `exit 0`. Quiet mode changes only the writer choice, so every value the line carries is the value the report already carries.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `recommend-level.sh` argument parser | Accepts 11 flags and rejects every other token with exit 1 | update: add `--quiet` after the `--json|-j` branch at `recommend-level.sh:706-709` | `grep -n -- '--quiet' recommend-level.sh` shows the case branch; `--quiet` run exits 0 |\n| `output_text` | Prints the 16-17 line report | unchanged | byte diff against `scratch/baseline/text-*.txt` |\n| `output_json` | Prints the JSON document | unchanged | byte diff against `scratch/baseline/json-*.json` |\n| new `output_quiet` | Prints one line | create beside `output_text` at `recommend-level.sh:508` | harness asserts exact content, line count and no leading blank line |\n| dispatch tail | Chooses text or JSON | update: quiet branch first at `recommend-level.sh:770-774` | `--quiet --json` harness case |\n| `show_help` OPTIONS | Lists the flags | update at `recommend-level.sh:181` | `bash recommend-level.sh --help \\| grep -c -- '--quiet'` returns `1` |\n| header comment OPTIONS | Lists the flags for readers of the file | update at `recommend-level.sh:26` | `grep -c -- '^#   --quiet' recommend-level.sh` returns `1` |\n| `execution-methods.md` flag table | Documents the scoring flags | update one row | `grep -c -- '--quiet' execution-methods.md` returns `1` |\n| In-repo callers of the script | None read its stdout | not a consumer | `grep -rn \"Recommended Level\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit` returns 0 hits outside `recommend-level.sh` |\n| `-q` short flag | Not present; `-q` exits 1 as unknown | unchanged | ADR-003; harness asserts `-q` still fails |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `grep -rln \"QUIET_MODE\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/*.sh` returns `check-completion.sh`, `progressive-validate.sh` and `validate.sh`. Each owns its own parser; there is no shared flag table, so this change adds one branch to one parser rather than updating a central list.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `grep -rn \"Recommended Level\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit` returns 0 hits outside `recommend-level.sh`, so no in-repo script parses the line.\n- Matrix axes: output mode (text, json, quiet, quiet+json) crossed with phase scoring (on, off) gives 8 rows; level boundaries (0, 1, 3) add 3 rows in quiet mode. The harness covers all 11.\n- Algorithm invariant: quiet mode selects a writer and must not alter any computed value. Adversarial cases: a leading blank line, an extra trailing line, JSON leaking through, a diagnostic leaking to stdout, and an unknown option being swallowed.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\n### Phase 1: Baseline capture\nRun the current script for the three level-boundary argument sets and store stdout in `scratch/baseline/`. Nothing changes until those files exist, because every later regression claim compares against them.\n\n### Phase 2: Parser and output function\nAdd `QUIET_MODE=false` beside `JSON_OUTPUT=false`, the `--quiet` case branch after `--json|-j`, and `output_quiet()` beside `output_text`. The function prints one line through a single `printf '%s\\n'`, which rules out the leading blank line `output_text` starts with.\n\n### Phase 3: Dispatch and help\nReorder the dispatch tail so quiet mode is checked before JSON, then document the flag in both help surfaces: the header comment and `show_help()`.\n\n### Phase 4: Verification\nWrite and run `runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh`, diff both default captures, and run `shellcheck` on the script.\n\n### Phase 5: Documentation and closeout\nAdd the `--quiet` row to `execution-methods.md`, update `tasks.md` evidence, and record the outcome in `implementation-summary.md` at completion time.\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the task state and the verification checklist.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | `output_quiet` output shape and the parser branch | `runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh` |\n| Regression | Default text and JSON output, byte for byte | `diff` against `scratch/baseline/` |\n| Integration | Combined flags and exit codes in one shell | Harness cases for `--quiet --json`, `--quiet --help`, `--quiet --bogus` |\n| Manual | Read the help text and run one example by hand | Terminal |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| Bash 3.2 or newer | External | Green | The script stops running on macOS's default shell |\n| `test-upgrade-level.sh` harness pattern | Internal | Green | The new harness invents its own summary format and is harder to compare |\n| `shellcheck` | External tooling | Green | Lint step is skipped; the harness still gates behavior |\n| `scratch/baseline/` captures | Internal | Green | AC-003 and AC-004 lose their before-picture |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: Default text or JSON output changes, or quiet output is anything other than exactly one line.\n- **Procedure**: Revert the single implementation commit. The change is confined to one script, one new test file and one documentation row; there is no data, schema or configuration to unwind.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Baseline) ──► Phase 2 (Parser + writer) ──► Phase 3 (Dispatch + help)\n                                                              │\n                                                              ▼\n                                              Phase 4 (Verify) ──► Phase 5 (Docs)\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Baseline | None | Parser + writer |\n| Parser + writer | Baseline | Dispatch + help |\n| Dispatch + help | Parser + writer | Verify |\n| Verify | Dispatch + help | Docs |\n| Docs | Verify | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Baseline capture | Low | 15 minutes |\n| Parser + writer | Low | 30 minutes |\n| Dispatch + help | Low | 15 minutes |\n| Verification | Medium | 25 minutes |\n| Documentation | Low | 10 minutes |\n| **Total** | | **About 1.5 hours** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [x] No data changes; nothing to back up\n- [x] No feature flag to configure; the new flag is itself the opt-in\n- [x] No monitoring change; this is CLI stdout only\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. `git revert <implementation-sha>` on the branch that carries the change.\n2. Re-run `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh`.\n3. Confirm the default captures still diff clean against `scratch/baseline/`.\n4. No stakeholder notification is needed; the script is internal tooling.\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No.\n- **Reversal procedure**: N/A\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│  Baseline   │     │ Parser+Writer│    │ Dispatch+Help│\n└─────────────┘     └─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘\n                                               │\n                                        ┌──────▼──────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n                                        │   Phase 4   │────►│   Phase 5   │\n                                        │   Verify    │     │    Docs     │\n                                        └─────────────┘     └─────────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline captures | None | Text and JSON reference output | Harness regression cases |\n| `QUIET_MODE` global and parser branch | Baseline | Accepted `--quiet` | `output_quiet` dispatch |\n| `output_quiet` | Parser branch | One-line writer | Dispatch |\n| Dispatch branch | `output_quiet` | Quiet selection | Harness, help verification |\n| Help text | Parser branch | Documented flag | Help assertions |\n| Harness | All implementation pieces | PASS/FAIL evidence | Packet closure |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **T001 Baseline capture** - 15 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **T003 `output_quiet`** - 20 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **T004 Dispatch branch** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n4. **T007 Harness** - 25 minutes - CRITICAL\n5. **T010 Strict validation of this packet** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: About 80 minutes\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- T005 help text and T012 documentation row can run alongside the harness.\n- T001 baseline capture can run before any edit and does not block the parser edit.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Baseline captured | `scratch/baseline/` holds text and JSON captures for three argument sets | Phase 1 |\n| M2 | Quiet mode implemented | `--quiet` prints one line; default paths untouched | Phase 3 |\n| M3 | Verified | Harness exits 0, default diffs clean, `shellcheck` clean | Phase 4 |\n| M4 | Documented and closeable | `execution-methods.md` updated; every acceptance row `Met` | Phase 5 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: Quiet output reuses the existing level line verbatim\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: A caller needs the recommended level, and the report already carries it as `Recommended Level: N (Name)`. Any second format would become a second contract to keep in sync.\n\n**Decision**: `output_quiet()` prints the same `Recommended Level: N (Name)` line that `output_text` prints, followed by one newline, with no leading blank line.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Positive: one grep pattern works against both the report and the quiet output; no new vocabulary.\n- Negative: machine consumers still split on `:` and `(`. That cost already exists for the report, and the level number and name stay readable.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Print only the integer: hides the level name and breaks the line callers already match.\n- Keep the report and let callers filter it: that is the status quo this packet removes.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-002: `--quiet` takes precedence over `--json`\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: Both flags request a specific output shape, and the script accepts flags in any order. Combining them has no obvious meaning.\n\n**Decision**: Quiet mode wins. `--quiet --json` prints the one-line level and no JSON document.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Positive: the flag's promise is unconditional, so no combination silently produces a different shape.\n- Negative: a caller that passed both by mistake loses JSON without an error. The help text states the precedence, and AC-005 pins it.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Error on the combination: adds a failure mode for a case with an obvious reading.\n- JSON wins: contradicts the flag's stated contract.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-003: No `-q` short alias in this packet\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: `validate.sh`, `check-completion.sh` and `progressive-validate.sh` accept `--quiet|-q`. Adding `-q` here would match them, but no caller has asked for it.\n\n**Decision**: Add only `--quiet`, the requested surface.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Positive: the surface stays exactly as large as the feature, and no short flag is claimed before its meaning is needed.\n- Negative: a user who types `-q` gets an unknown-option error, which is inconsistent with the sibling scripts. A later packet can add the alias with a caller behind it.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Add `-q` now: unrequested surface, and the harness would then need to pin an alias nothing uses.\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":1}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
