{"toolCallId":"call_cb732563f2e7443c8be691f9e5236e78","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.2 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | [e.g., TypeScript, Python 3.11] |\n| **Framework** | [e.g., React, FastAPI] |\n| **Storage** | [e.g., PostgreSQL, None] |\n| **Testing** | [e.g., Jest, pytest] |\n\n### Overview\n[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\n[MVC | MVVM | Clean Architecture | Serverless | Monolith | Other]\n\n### Key Components\n- **[Component 1]**: [Purpose]\n- **[Component 2]**: [Purpose]\n\n### Data Flow\n[Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\nUse this section when `research_intent=fix_bug`, when planning from a deep-review FAIL/CONDITIONAL verdict, or when any finding touches security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, public responses, or shared policy.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| [producer/helper/policy] | [what owns the behavior] | [update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [grep/test/doc evidence] |\n| [consumer/status/docs/tests] | [how it observes the behavior] | [update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [grep/test/doc evidence] |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n '<field|string|helper|literal|error-pattern>' <module-or-files>`.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n '<changedSymbol>|<changedConstant>|<changedPublicField>' . --glob '*.ts' --glob '*.js' --glob '*.md'`.\n- Matrix axes: list every independent input axis and the required rows before implementation.\n- Algorithm invariant: for path/redaction/parser/resolver/security fixes, state the invariant and adversarial cases.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | [Components/functions] | [Jest/pytest/etc.] |\n| Integration | [API endpoints/flows] | [Tools] |\n| Manual | [User journeys] | Browser |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| [System/Library] | [Internal/External] | [Green/Yellow/Red] | [Impact] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: [Conditions requiring rollback]\n- **Procedure**: [How to revert changes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────┐\n                      ├──► Phase 2 (Core) ──► Phase 3 (Verify)\nPhase 1.5 (Config) ───┘\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Core, Config |\n| Config | Setup | Core |\n| Core | Setup, Config | Verify |\n| Verify | Core | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | [Low/Med/High] | [e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| Core Implementation | [Low/Med/High] | [e.g., 4-8 hours] |\n| Verification | [Low/Med/High] | [e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| **Total** | | **[e.g., 6-12 hours]** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes)\n- [ ] Feature flag configured\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. [Immediate action - e.g., disable feature flag]\n2. [Revert code - e.g., git revert or redeploy previous version]\n3. [Verify rollback - e.g., smoke test critical paths]\n4. [Notify stakeholders - if user-facing]\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** [Yes/No]\n- **Reversal procedure**: [Steps or \"N/A\"]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘     └─────────────┘\n                          │\n                    ┌─────▼─────┐\n                    │  Phase 2b │\n                    │  Parallel │\n                    └───────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| [Component A] | None | [Output] | B, C |\n| [Component B] | A | [Output] | D |\n| [Component C] | A | [Output] | D |\n| [Component D] | B, C | [Final] | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **[Phase/Task]** - [Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n2. **[Phase/Task]** - [Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n3. **[Phase/Task]** - [Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: [Sum of durations]\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- [Task A] and [Task B] can run simultaneously\n- [Task C] and [Task D] can run after Phase 1\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | [Setup Complete] | [All dependencies ready] | [Date/Phase] |\n| M2 | [Core Done] | [Main features working] | [Date/Phase] |\n| M3 | [Release Ready] | [All tests pass] | [Date/Phase] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: [Decision Title]\n\n**Status**: [Proposed/Accepted/Deprecated]\n\n**Context**: [What problem we're solving]\n\n**Decision**: [What we decided]\n\n**Consequences**:\n- [Positive outcome 1]\n- [Negative outcome + mitigation]\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- [Option B]: [Why rejected]\n\n---\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add a third output mode to recommend-level.sh: a --quiet flag that prints only the Recommended Level line. The change touches the argument parser, one new output function and the dispatch tail; scoring is untouched.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.2 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2-compatible shell |\n| **Framework** | None; one script, no sourced project library |\n| **Storage** | None |\n| **Testing** | Bash harness in `runtime/cli/tests/`, byte-diff captures, and `shellcheck` at `/opt/homebrew/bin/shellcheck` |\n\n### Overview\n`recommend-level.sh` already separates scoring from presentation: the scoring functions fill globals, and a dispatch tail chooses `output_text` or `output_json`. This change adds a third writer, `output_quiet`, and a `QUIET_MODE` global set by a `--quiet` case branch. The dispatch checks quiet first, so the flag prints the same level line the text report carries and nothing else. No scoring function changes.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [x] Problem statement and scope documented in `spec.md` §2 and §3\n- [x] Success criteria measurable in `spec.md` §5 and `acceptance-criteria.md`\n- [x] Dependencies identified in §6 of this plan\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh` exits 0 with zero failures\n- [ ] Default text and JSON captures diff clean against `scratch/baseline/`\n- [ ] Spec, plan and tasks agree on the final behavior\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nSingle-file CLI script with a dispatch tail. There is no framework, no service layer and no stored state; the script computes in memory and writes once.\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument parser** (`recommend-level.sh:646-719`): a `while`/`case` loop that sets `LOC`, `FILES` and the risk flags and rejects unknown options. It gains the `--quiet` branch.\n- **Scoring pipeline** (`recommend-level.sh:228-500`): `calculate_loc_score`, `calculate_files_score`, `calculate_risk_score`, `calculate_complexity_score`, `determine_level`, `calculate_confidence`, `determine_phasing`. Unchanged.\n- **Output writers** (`recommend-level.sh:508-637`): `output_text` and `output_json` today; this packet adds `output_quiet` beside them.\n- **Dispatch tail** (`recommend-level.sh:770-774`): selects one writer and exits 0. This is the only control-flow change.\n\n### Data Flow\n`argv` → parser sets inputs and mode globals → scoring fills `TOTAL_SCORE`, `RECOMMENDED_LEVEL`, `LEVEL_NAME`, `CONFIDENCE` and the phase fields → dispatch picks one writer → stdout → `exit 0`. Quiet mode changes only the writer choice, so every value the line carries is the value the report already carries.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `recommend-level.sh` argument parser | Accepts 11 flags and rejects every other token with exit 1 | update: add `--quiet` after the `--json|-j` branch at `recommend-level.sh:706-709` | `grep -n -- '--quiet' recommend-level.sh` shows the case branch; `--quiet` run exits 0 |\n| `output_text` | Prints the 16-17 line report | unchanged | byte diff against `scratch/baseline/text-*.txt` |\n| `output_json` | Prints the JSON document | unchanged | byte diff against `scratch/baseline/json-*.json` |\n| new `output_quiet` | Prints one line | create beside `output_text` at `recommend-level.sh:508` | harness asserts exact content, line count and no leading blank line |\n| dispatch tail | Chooses text or JSON | update: quiet branch first at `recommend-level.sh:770-774` | `--quiet --json` harness case |\n| `show_help` OPTIONS | Lists the flags | update at `recommend-level.sh:181` | `bash recommend-level.sh --help \\| grep -c -- '--quiet'` returns `1` |\n| header comment OPTIONS | Lists the flags for readers of the file | update at `recommend-level.sh:26` | `grep -c -- '^#   --quiet' recommend-level.sh` returns `1` |\n| `execution-methods.md` flag table | Documents the scoring flags | update one row | `grep -c -- '--quiet' execution-methods.md` returns `1` |\n| In-repo callers of the script | None read its stdout | not a consumer | `grep -rn \"Recommended Level\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit` returns 0 hits outside `recommend-level.sh` |\n| `-q` short flag | Not present; `-q` exits 1 as unknown | unchanged | ADR-003; harness asserts `-q` still fails |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `grep -rln \"QUIET_MODE\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/*.sh` returns `check-completion.sh`, `progressive-validate.sh` and `validate.sh`. Each owns its own parser; there is no shared flag table, so this change adds one branch to one parser rather than updating a central list.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `grep -rn \"Recommended Level\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit` returns 0 hits outside `recommend-level.sh`, so no in-repo script parses the line.\n- Matrix axes: output mode (text, json, quiet, quiet+json) crossed with phase scoring (on, off) gives 8 rows; level boundaries (0, 1, 3) add 3 rows in quiet mode. The harness covers all 11.\n- Algorithm invariant: quiet mode selects a writer and must not alter any computed value. Adversarial cases: a leading blank line, an extra trailing line, JSON leaking through, a diagnostic leaking to stdout, and an unknown option being swallowed.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\n### Phase 1: Baseline capture\nRun the current script for the three level-boundary argument sets and store stdout in `scratch/baseline/`. Nothing changes until those files exist, because every later regression claim compares against them.\n\n### Phase 2: Parser and output function\nAdd `QUIET_MODE=false` beside `JSON_OUTPUT=false`, the `--quiet` case branch after `--json|-j`, and `output_quiet()` beside `output_text`. The function prints one line through a single `printf '%s\\n'`, which rules out the leading blank line `output_text` starts with.\n\n### Phase 3: Dispatch and help\nReorder the dispatch tail so quiet mode is checked before JSON, then document the flag in both help surfaces: the header comment and `show_help()`.\n\n### Phase 4: Verification\nWrite and run `runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh`, diff both default captures, and run `shellcheck` on the script.\n\n### Phase 5: Documentation and closeout\nAdd the `--quiet` row to `execution-methods.md`, update `tasks.md` evidence, and record the outcome in `implementation-summary.md` at completion time.\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the task state and the verification checklist.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | `output_quiet` output shape and the parser branch | `runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh` |\n| Regression | Default text and JSON output, byte for byte | `diff` against `scratch/baseline/` |\n| Integration | Combined flags and exit codes in one shell | Harness cases for `--quiet --json`, `--quiet --help`, `--quiet --bogus` |\n| Manual | Read the help text and run one example by hand | Terminal |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| Bash 3.2 or newer | External | Green | The script stops running on macOS's default shell |\n| `test-upgrade-level.sh` harness pattern | Internal | Green | The new harness invents its own summary format and is harder to compare |\n| `shellcheck` | External tooling | Green | Lint step is skipped; the harness still gates behavior |\n| `scratch/baseline/` captures | Internal | Green | AC-003 and AC-004 lose their before-picture |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: Default text or JSON output changes, or quiet output is anything other than exactly one line.\n- **Procedure**: Revert the single implementation commit. The change is confined to one script, one new test file and one documentation row; there is no data, schema or configuration to unwind.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Baseline) ──► Phase 2 (Parser + writer) ──► Phase 3 (Dispatch + help)\n                                                              │\n                                                              ▼\n                                              Phase 4 (Verify) ──► Phase 5 (Docs)\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Baseline | None | Parser + writer, Docs |\n| Parser + writer | Baseline | Dispatch + help |\n| Dispatch + help | Parser + writer | Verify |\n| Verify | Dispatch + help | Docs |\n| Docs | Verify | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Baseline capture | Low | 15 minutes |\n| Parser + writer | Low | 30 minutes |\n| Dispatch + help | Low | 15 minutes |\n| Verification | Medium | 25 minutes |\n| Documentation | Low | 10 minutes |\n| **Total** | | **About 1.5 hours** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [x] No data changes; nothing to back up\n- [x] No feature flag to configure; the new flag is itself the opt-in\n- [x] No monitoring change; this is CLI stdout only\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. `git revert <implementation-sha>` on the branch that carries the change.\n2. Re-run `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh`.\n3. Confirm the default captures still diff clean against `scratch/baseline/`.\n4. No stakeholder notification is needed; the script is internal tooling.\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No.\n- **Reversal procedure**: N/A\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│  Baseline   │     │ Parser+Writer│    │ Dispatch+Help│\n└─────────────┘     └─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘\n                                               │\n                                        ┌──────▼──────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n                                        │   Phase 4   │────►│   Phase 5   │\n                                        │   Verify    │     │    Docs     │\n                                        └─────────────┘     └─────────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline captures | None | Text and JSON reference output | Harness regression cases |\n| `QUIET_MODE` global and parser branch | Baseline | Accepted `--quiet` | `output_quiet` dispatch |\n| `output_quiet` | Parser branch | One-line writer | Dispatch |\n| Dispatch branch | `output_quiet` | Quiet selection | Harness, help verification |\n| Help text | Parser branch | Documented flag | Help assertions |\n| Harness | All implementation pieces | PASS/FAIL evidence | Packet closure |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **T001 Baseline capture** - 15 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **T003 `output_quiet`** - 20 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **T004 Dispatch branch** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n4. **T007 Harness** - 25 minutes - CRITICAL\n5. **T010 Strict validation of this packet** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: About 80 minutes\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- T005 help text and T012 documentation row can run alongside the harness.\n- T001 baseline capture can run before any edit and does not block the parser edit.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Baseline captured | `scratch/baseline/` holds text and JSON captures for three argument sets | Phase 1 |\n| M2 | Quiet mode implemented | `--quiet` prints one line; default paths untouched | Phase 3 |\n| M3 | Verified | Harness exits 0, default diffs clean, `shellcheck` clean | Phase 4 |\n| M4 | Documented and closeable | `execution-methods.md` updated; every acceptance row `Met` | Phase 5 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: Quiet output reuses the existing level line verbatim\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: A caller needs the recommended level, and the report already carries it as `Recommended Level: N (Name)`. Any second format would become a second contract to keep in sync.\n\n**Decision**: `output_quiet()` prints the same `Recommended Level: N (Name)` line that `output_text` prints, followed by one newline, with no leading blank line.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Positive: one grep pattern works against both the report and the quiet output; no new vocabulary.\n- Negative: machine consumers still split on `:` and `(`. That cost already exists for the report, and the level number and name stay readable.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Print only the integer: hides the level name and breaks the line callers already match.\n- Keep the report and let callers filter it: that is the status quo this packet removes.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-002: `--quiet` takes precedence over `--json`\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: Both flags request a specific output shape, and the script accepts flags in any order. Combining them has no obvious meaning.\n\n**Decision**: Quiet mode wins. `--quiet --json` prints the one-line level and no JSON document.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Positive: the flag's promise is unconditional, so no combination silently produces a different shape.\n- Negative: a caller that passed both by mistake loses JSON without an error. The help text states the precedence, and AC-005 pins it.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Error on the combination: adds a failure mode for a case with an obvious reading.\n- JSON wins: contradicts the flag's stated contract.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-003: No `-q` short alias in this packet\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: `validate.sh`, `check-completion.sh` and `progressive-validate.sh` accept `--quiet|-q`. Adding `-q` here would match them, but no caller has asked for it.\n\n**Decision**: Add only `--quiet`, the requested surface.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Positive: the surface stays exactly as large as the feature, and no short flag is claimed before its meaning is needed.\n- Negative: a user who types `-q` gets an unknown-option error, which is inconsistent with the sibling scripts. A later packet can add the alias with a caller behind it.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Add `-q` now: unrequested surface, and the harness would then need to pin an alias nothing uses.\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":151,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":77}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_ce45c6f50a9342388c90aa9b4d6c5352","title":"Ran bash","kind":"execute","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"resource","resource":{"mimeType":"text/x-shellscript","text":"bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh --skip-branch --level 3 --track zz-bench-authoring --short-name recommend-level-quiet-flag \"Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"","uri":"tool://preview"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/preview_is_shell_command":true}}}],"rawInput":{"command":"bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh --skip-branch --level 3 --track zz-bench-authoring --short-name recommend-level-quiet-flag \"Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"","workdir":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","timeout":120000},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timeoutMs":120000,"cognition.ai/commandNames":["bash"],"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_d09a978587e94cba97b46a006f9b5976","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Ordered work for the --quiet flag: baseline capture, parser and writer, dispatch and help, verification, documentation.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`, followed by a `File:` line, a `Change:` line, a fenced `Check:` block with its `Expected:` result, a `Rollback:` line and a `Stop and escalate if:` line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ai-exec -->\n## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\nBefore starting a task, verify:\n1. The task's `File:` line names a path that exists, or its parent directory does.\n2. `scratch/baseline/` exists before any script edit; without it, AC-003 and AC-004 cannot be met.\n3. The current script still prints `ERROR: Unknown option: --quiet`; if it does not, the flag already exists and this packet's premise is stale.\n4. No task edits a file outside the three paths in `spec.md` §3.\n\n### Execution Rules\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| TASK-SEQ | Complete tasks in order; T001 must finish before any edit. |\n| TASK-SCOPE | Touch only `recommend-level.sh`, the new `test-recommend-level.sh`, and one row of `execution-methods.md`. |\n| TASK-VERIFY | Every edit is followed by its `Check:` block, and the expected result is read, not assumed. |\n| TASK-DOC | Update this file's checkboxes and the packet's acceptance rows as evidence lands. |\n| TASK-ONE-WRITER | Quiet mode selects an existing writer path; never duplicate the level-line formatting in a second place. |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\nAfter each task: `Task T### complete. Files modified: <list>. Check: <result>.`\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\nIf a check fails twice, stop, write the failing command and its output into this file under the task, mark the task `[B]`, and escalate. Do not widen scope to make a check pass.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ai-exec -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Baseline capture\n\n### T001 Capture the pre-change output for every mode and phase setting (AC-003, AC-004)\n\nFile: `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/baseline/` (new directory).\n\nChange: six captures that AC-003 and AC-004 diff against. Phase-on text is 16 lines at Level 1 and 17 at Level 3; phase-off text is 12 lines; phase-on JSON is 36 lines; phase-off JSON is 32 lines.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\ncd \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\"\nB=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/baseline\nS=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nmkdir -p \"$B\"\nbash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 > \"$B/text-level0.txt\"\nbash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api > \"$B/text-level1.txt\"\nbash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural > \"$B/text-level3.txt\"\nbash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --no-recommend-phases > \"$B/text-level1-nophase.txt\"\nbash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --json > \"$B/json-level1.json\"\nbash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --json --no-recommend-phases > \"$B/json-level1-nophase.json\"\nwc -l \"$B/text-level0.txt\" \"$B/text-level1.txt\" \"$B/text-level3.txt\" \"$B/text-level1-nophase.txt\" \"$B/json-level1.json\" \"$B/json-level1-nophase.json\"\nsed -n '1,2p' \"$B/text-level1.txt\"\n```\n\nExpected: line counts `16`, `16`, `17`, `12`, `36`, `32` in the order written; `sed` prints an empty line followed by `Recommended Level: 1 (Baseline)`.\n\nRollback: delete `scratch/baseline/`.\n\nStop and escalate if: any capture is empty, or the level line is not on line 2 of a text capture.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Parser and output function\n\n### T002 Add the quiet-mode global (REQ-001)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:122`. Anchor: the line `JSON_OUTPUT=false`.\n\nChange: add `QUIET_MODE=false` directly below `JSON_OUTPUT=false`, in the same defaults block, so every mode flag is declared in one place.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\ngrep -n 'QUIET_MODE=false' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\n```\n\nExpected: one hit at line 123.\n\nRollback: delete the line.\n\nStop and escalate if: the defaults block no longer contains `JSON_OUTPUT=false`.\n\n---\n\n### T003 Add the `--quiet` case branch (REQ-001)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:706-709`. Anchor: the `--json|-j)` branch.\n\nChange: add a `--quiet)` branch after the JSON branch that sets `QUIET_MODE=true` and runs `shift`.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet\necho \"EXIT=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: exit 0. Before T004 lands the output may still be the full report; the acceptance criterion for one-line output is T004 and T006.\n\nRollback: delete the branch.\n\nStop and escalate if: the parser still reports `ERROR: Unknown option: --quiet`.\n\n---\n\n### T004 Add `output_quiet()` (REQ-002)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:508`. Anchor: the `output_text()` function header.\n\nChange: add a writer that prints exactly one line through `printf '%s\\n' \"Recommended Level: ${RECOMMENDED_LEVEL} (${LEVEL_NAME})\"`. Do not call `output_text` and filter it, and do not add a leading `echo \"\"`.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nsed -n '/^output_quiet()/,/^}/p' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\n```\n\nExpected: the function body contains one `printf '%s\\n'` line and no `echo`.\n\nRollback: delete the function.\n\nStop and escalate if: `RECOMMENDED_LEVEL` or `LEVEL_NAME` is not set before the writers run.\n\n---\n\n### T005 Document the flag in both help surfaces (REQ-005)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:26` and `:181`. Anchors: the header comment's `--json, -j` line and the same line inside `show_help()`.\n\nChange: add `--quiet` with the text `Print only the final recommended-level line` in both OPTIONS lists, and add one example to each EXAMPLES block showing `--quiet` with `--loc 200 --files 5 --api`.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\ngrep -c -- '^#   --quiet' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --help | grep -c -- '--quiet'\n```\n\nExpected: `1` and `1`.\n\nRollback: remove both lines and the examples.\n\nStop and escalate if: the two help surfaces have diverged beyond the flag line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Dispatch and help wiring\n\n### T006 Make quiet mode win in the dispatch tail (REQ-004)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:770-774`. Anchor: the `if [[ \"$JSON_OUTPUT\" = true ]]; then` block.\n\nChange: turn the two-way dispatch into a three-way choice with quiet checked first: quiet, then JSON, then text.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --loc 200 --files 5 --api --quiet --json\necho \"EXIT=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: exactly `Recommended Level: 1 (Baseline)` and `EXIT=0`; no `{`.\n\nRollback: restore the two-way dispatch.\n\nStop and escalate if: `--json` alone stops producing JSON.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-4 -->\n## Phase 4: Verification\n\n### T007 Write the harness (REQ-009)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh` (new).\n\nChange: follow the `test-upgrade-level.sh` shape: `set -euo pipefail`, `pass`/`fail`/`skip` counters, a `Results: N passed, N failed, N skipped (of N)` summary on stderr, and exit 1 when `FAIL` is non-zero. Cover 15 assertions: the 10 matrix rows from `plan.md` (8 mode/phase combinations plus the Level 0 and Level 3 quiet lines) and 5 guards (`--quiet --help`, `--quiet --bogus`, `--quiet` with no inputs, `-q`, and an explicit one-line/no-leading-blank check on the Level 1 quiet run).\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nbash -n .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh\n```\n\nExpected: exit 0, no syntax error.\n\nRollback: delete the file.\n\nStop and escalate if: the harness needs a fixture outside `scratch/baseline/`.\n\n---\n\n### T008 Run the harness (AC-010)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh`.\n\nChange: none; this task records the run.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh\necho \"EXIT=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: `Results: 15 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (of 15)` and `EXIT=0`.\n\nRollback: none.\n\nStop and escalate if: any assertion fails; fix the implementation, not the assertion, unless the assertion contradicts `acceptance-criteria.md`.\n\n---\n\n### T009 Diff both default output paths against the baseline (AC-003, AC-004)\n\nFile: `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/baseline/`.\n\nChange: none; this task proves the no-change claim.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nB=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/baseline\nS=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\ndiff \"$B/text-level0.txt\" <(bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2)\ndiff \"$B/text-level1.txt\" <(bash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api)\ndiff \"$B/text-level3.txt\" <(bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural)\ndiff \"$B/text-level1-nophase.txt\" <(bash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --no-recommend-phases)\ndiff \"$B/json-level1.json\" <(bash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --json)\ndiff \"$B/json-level1-nophase.json\" <(bash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --json --no-recommend-phases)\necho \"DIFFS_CLEAN=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: no diff output and `DIFFS_CLEAN=0`.\n\nRollback: none.\n\nStop and escalate if: any diff shows a line, including whitespace-only changes.\n\n---\n\n### T010 Lint the script (CHK-010)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`.\n\nChange: none; this task records the lint result.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nshellcheck .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\necho \"EXIT=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: `EXIT=0`. If the pre-change script already reports findings, record the pre-change count in `scratch/` and require that the change adds none.\n\nRollback: none.\n\nStop and escalate if: the new function adds a finding that cannot be fixed without touching scoring code.\n\n---\n\n### T011 Validate this packet strictly (CHK-020)\n\nFile: `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/`.\n\nChange: none; this task records the packet gate.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag --strict\n```\n\nExpected: `RESULT: PASSED` with zero errors.\n\nRollback: none.\n\nStop and escalate if: validation reports an error outside the three files this packet changes.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-4 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-5 -->\n## Phase 5: Documentation and closeout\n\n### T012 Document the flag in the workflow reference (REQ-010)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/execution-methods.md`. Anchor: the `**Feature Flags:**` table in §6.\n\nChange: add one row, `--quiet | Print only the final recommended-level line`. Leave the stale positional examples alone; they are a separate defect recorded in `spec.md` §3.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\ngrep -c -- '--quiet' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/execution-methods.md\n```\n\nExpected: `1`.\n\nRollback: delete the row.\n\nStop and escalate if: the flag table has moved or been rewritten by another packet.\n\n---\n\n### T013 Close the packet (AC-001 through AC-011)\n\nFile: `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/`.\n\nChange: mark every acceptance row `Met` with its evidence, check the tasks and verification items that ran, and record the outcome in `implementation-summary.md`.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag --strict\n```\n\nExpected: `RESULT: PASSED` and every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` reads `Met` with a `file:line` or command result.\n\nRollback: none.\n\nStop and escalate if: a criterion cannot be met and no ADR exists to waive it.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-5 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Acceptance Criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Baseline captures exist in `scratch/baseline/` before the first edit\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `shellcheck` passes on `recommend-level.sh`, or the change adds no finding to the pre-change count\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] Quiet output goes through one `printf` and no `echo`\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] The new function follows the file's comment and naming style\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] No scoring function changed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] `bash runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh` exits 0 with zero failures\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] All six baseline captures diff clean\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Combined flags behave as specified: `--quiet --json`, `--quiet --help`, `--quiet --no-recommend-phases`, `--quiet --bogus`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Finding class recorded: `instance-only` for the flag surface, because one parser owns it and no shared flag table exists.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory run: `grep -rln \"QUIET_MODE\" runtime/cli/spec/*.sh` names `check-completion.sh`, `progressive-validate.sh` and `validate.sh`; none shares a parser with `recommend-level.sh`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory run: `grep -rn \"Recommended Level\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit` returns no hit outside `recommend-level.sh`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Adversarial table run: leading blank line, extra trailing line, JSON leakage, stdout leakage from errors, unknown option swallowed. All five are harness cases.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count listed in `plan.md` FIX ADDENDUM: 8 mode/phase rows plus 3 level rows.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Hostile environment variant: run the harness with `LC_ALL=C`; the script reads no process-wide state.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence pinned to the implementation commit SHA, not a moving branch range.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets in the script or harness\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Unknown options are still rejected with exit 1\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] No auth or authorization surface exists in this script, so no authz check applies\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec, plan, tasks and acceptance criteria agree on the final behavior\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The new function carries the same comment header style as its neighbors\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] README table entry for `recommend-level.sh` needs no change; confirm and record\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temporary captures live in `scratch/baseline/` only\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/baseline/` is retained as AC-003 and AC-004 evidence; every other temp file is removed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 15 | 0/15 |\n| P1 Items | 24 | 0/24 |\n| P2 Items | 8 | 0/8 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-26\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] Architecture decisions documented as ADR-001 through ADR-003 in `plan.md`\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] Every ADR carries a status; all three are `Accepted`\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives are documented with rejection rationale\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] Migration path is N/A: the script has no stored data and no configuration to migrate\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] Quiet run wall time is at or below the default run for the same inputs, measured with `time`\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] Throughput target is N/A: the script is invoked once per task, not in a loop\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] Load testing is N/A: no service or concurrent path exists\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] The timing pair is recorded in `implementation-summary.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented in `plan.md` §7 and exercised by a revert in a scratch clone\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] No feature flag is required; `--quiet` is itself the opt-in\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] Monitoring is N/A: the script writes to stdout only and emits no metrics\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] Runbook is N/A: no deployment step exists beyond merging the commit\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] Deployment review is N/A for the same reason\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review is N/A: no auth, network, filesystem write or secret surface changes\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] No dependency is added, so no license changes\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] OWASP checklist is N/A: no web surface\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] Data handling is N/A: the script stores nothing\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation is N/A: the script exposes a CLI, documented in its help text\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] `execution-methods.md` carries the new flag row\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer is N/A: the change is one flag and one function\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| Packet author | Planning | Pending | |\n| Reviewer | sk-code review | Pending | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Ordered work for the --quiet flag: baseline capture, parser and writer, dispatch and help, verification, documentation.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`, followed by a `File:` line, a `Change:` line, a fenced `Check:` block with its `Expected:` result, a `Rollback:` line and a `Stop and escalate if:` line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ai-exec -->\n## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\nBefore starting a task, verify:\n1. The task's `File:` line names a path that exists, or its parent directory does.\n2. `scratch/baseline/` exists before any script edit; without it, AC-003 and AC-004 cannot be met.\n3. The current script still prints `ERROR: Unknown option: --quiet`; if it does not, the flag already exists and this packet's premise is stale.\n4. No task edits a file outside the three paths in `spec.md` §3.\n\n### Execution Rules\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| TASK-SEQ | Complete tasks in order; T001 must finish before any edit. |\n| TASK-SCOPE | Touch only `recommend-level.sh`, the new `test-recommend-level.sh`, and one row of `execution-methods.md`. |\n| TASK-VERIFY | Every edit is followed by its `Check:` block, and the expected result is read, not assumed. |\n| TASK-DOC | Update this file's checkboxes and the packet's acceptance rows as evidence lands. |\n| TASK-ONE-WRITER | Quiet mode selects an existing writer path; never duplicate the level-line formatting in a second place. |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\nAfter each task: `Task T### complete. Files modified: <list>. Check: <result>.`\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\nIf a check fails twice, stop, write the failing command and its output into this file under the task, mark the task `[B]`, and escalate. Do not widen scope to make a check pass.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ai-exec -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Baseline capture\n\n### T001 Capture the pre-change output for every mode and phase setting (AC-003, AC-004)\n\nFile: `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/baseline/` (new directory).\n\nChange: six captures that AC-003 and AC-004 diff against. Phase-on text is 16 lines at Level 1 and 17 at Level 3; phase-off text is 12 lines; phase-on JSON is 36 lines; phase-off JSON is 32 lines.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\ncd \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\"\nB=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/baseline\nS=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nmkdir -p \"$B\"\nbash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 > \"$B/text-level0.txt\"\nbash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api > \"$B/text-level1.txt\"\nbash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural > \"$B/text-level3.txt\"\nbash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --no-recommend-phases > \"$B/text-level1-nophase.txt\"\nbash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --json > \"$B/json-level1.json\"\nbash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --json --no-recommend-phases > \"$B/json-level1-nophase.json\"\nwc -l \"$B/text-level0.txt\" \"$B/text-level1.txt\" \"$B/text-level3.txt\" \"$B/text-level1-nophase.txt\" \"$B/json-level1.json\" \"$B/json-level1-nophase.json\"\nsed -n '1,2p' \"$B/text-level1.txt\"\n```\n\nExpected: line counts `16`, `16`, `17`, `12`, `36`, `32` in the order written; `sed` prints an empty line followed by `Recommended Level: 1 (Baseline)`.\n\nRollback: delete `scratch/baseline/`.\n\nStop and escalate if: any capture is empty, or the level line is not on line 2 of a text capture.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Parser and output function\n\n### T002 Add the quiet-mode global (REQ-001)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:122`. Anchor: the line `JSON_OUTPUT=false`.\n\nChange: add `QUIET_MODE=false` directly below `JSON_OUTPUT=false`, in the same defaults block, so every mode flag is declared in one place.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\ngrep -n 'QUIET_MODE=false' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\n```\n\nExpected: one hit at line 123.\n\nRollback: delete the line.\n\nStop and escalate if: the defaults block no longer contains `JSON_OUTPUT=false`.\n\n---\n\n### T003 Add the `--quiet` case branch (REQ-001)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:706-709`. Anchor: the `--json|-j)` branch.\n\nChange: add a `--quiet)` branch after the JSON branch that sets `QUIET_MODE=true` and runs `shift`.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet\necho \"EXIT=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: exit 0. Before T004 lands the output may still be the full report; the acceptance criterion for one-line output is T004 and T006.\n\nRollback: delete the branch.\n\nStop and escalate if: the parser still reports `ERROR: Unknown option: --quiet`.\n\n---\n\n### T004 Add `output_quiet()` (REQ-002)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:508`. Anchor: the `output_text()` function header.\n\nChange: add a writer that prints exactly one line through `printf '%s\\n' \"Recommended Level: ${RECOMMENDED_LEVEL} (${LEVEL_NAME})\"`. Do not call `output_text` and filter it, and do not add a leading `echo \"\"`.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nsed -n '/^output_quiet()/,/^}/p' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\n```\n\nExpected: the function body contains one `printf '%s\\n'` line and no `echo`.\n\nRollback: delete the function.\n\nStop and escalate if: `RECOMMENDED_LEVEL` or `LEVEL_NAME` is not set before the writers run.\n\n---\n\n### T005 Document the flag in both help surfaces (REQ-005)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:26` and `:181`. Anchors: the header comment's `--json, -j` line and the same line inside `show_help()`.\n\nChange: add `--quiet` with the text `Print only the final recommended-level line` in both OPTIONS lists, and add one example to each EXAMPLES block showing `--quiet` with `--loc 200 --files 5 --api`.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\ngrep -c -- '^#   --quiet' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --help | grep -c -- '--quiet'\n```\n\nExpected: `1` and `1`.\n\nRollback: remove both lines and the examples.\n\nStop and escalate if: the two help surfaces have diverged beyond the flag line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Dispatch and help wiring\n\n### T006 Make quiet mode win in the dispatch tail (REQ-004)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:770-774`. Anchor: the `if [[ \"$JSON_OUTPUT\" = true ]]; then` block.\n\nChange: turn the two-way dispatch into a three-way choice with quiet checked first: quiet, then JSON, then text.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --loc 200 --files 5 --api --quiet --json\necho \"EXIT=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: exactly `Recommended Level: 1 (Baseline)` and `EXIT=0`; no `{`.\n\nRollback: restore the two-way dispatch.\n\nStop and escalate if: `--json` alone stops producing JSON.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-4 -->\n## Phase 4: Verification\n\n### T007 Write the harness (REQ-009)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh` (new).\n\nChange: follow the `test-upgrade-level.sh` shape: `set -euo pipefail`, `pass`/`fail`/`skip` counters, a `Results: N passed, N failed, N skipped (of N)` summary on stderr, and exit 1 when `FAIL` is non-zero. Cover 15 assertions: the 10 matrix rows from `plan.md` (8 mode/phase combinations plus the Level 0 and Level 3 quiet lines) and 5 guards (`--quiet --help`, `--quiet --bogus`, `--quiet` with no inputs, `-q`, and an explicit one-line/no-leading-blank check on the Level 1 quiet run).\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nbash -n .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh\n```\n\nExpected: exit 0, no syntax error.\n\nRollback: delete the file.\n\nStop and escalate if: the harness needs a fixture outside `scratch/baseline/`.\n\n---\n\n### T008 Run the harness (AC-010)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh`.\n\nChange: none; this task records the run.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-recommend-level.sh\necho \"EXIT=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: `Results: 15 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (of 15)` and `EXIT=0`.\n\nRollback: none.\n\nStop and escalate if: any assertion fails; fix the implementation, not the assertion, unless the assertion contradicts `acceptance-criteria.md`.\n\n---\n\n### T009 Diff both default output paths against the baseline (AC-003, AC-004)\n\nFile: `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/baseline/`.\n\nChange: none; this task proves the no-change claim.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nB=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/baseline\nS=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\ndiff \"$B/text-level0.txt\" <(bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2)\ndiff \"$B/text-level1.txt\" <(bash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api)\ndiff \"$B/text-level3.txt\" <(bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural)\ndiff \"$B/text-level1-nophase.txt\" <(bash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --no-recommend-phases)\ndiff \"$B/json-level1.json\" <(bash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --json)\ndiff \"$B/json-level1-nophase.json\" <(bash \"$S\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --json --no-recommend-phases)\necho \"DIFFS_CLEAN=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: no diff output and `DIFFS_CLEAN=0`.\n\nRollback: none.\n\nStop and escalate if: any diff shows a line, including whitespace-only changes.\n\n---\n\n### T010 Lint the script (CHK-010)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`.\n\nChange: none; this task records the lint result.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nshellcheck .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\necho \"EXIT=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: `EXIT=0`. If the pre-change script already reports findings, record the pre-change count in `scratch/` and require that the change adds none.\n\nRollback: none.\n\nStop and escalate if: the new function adds a finding that cannot be fixed without touching scoring code.\n\n---\n\n### T011 Validate this packet strictly (CHK-020)\n\nFile: `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/`.\n\nChange: none; this task records the packet gate.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag --strict\n```\n\nExpected: `RESULT: PASSED` with zero errors.\n\nRollback: none.\n\nStop and escalate if: validation reports an error outside the three files this packet changes.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-4 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-5 -->\n## Phase 5: Documentation and closeout\n\n### T012 Document the flag in the workflow reference (REQ-010)\n\nFile: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/execution-methods.md`. Anchor: the `**Feature Flags:**` table in §6.\n\nChange: add one row, `--quiet | Print only the final recommended-level line`. Leave the stale positional example